1
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:37,159
Hello, comrades.

2
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:38,599
My name is Tan Yan.

3
00:01:40,079 --> 00:01:40,519
Loyalty,

4
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:42,719
dedication,

5
00:01:43,319 --> 00:01:43,680
bravery,

6
00:01:44,319 --> 00:01:44,799
and sacrifice.

7
00:01:46,599 --> 00:01:48,280
These are the fine traditions that Hongye

8
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:49,359
Municipal Police SWAT Detachment

9
00:01:50,079 --> 00:01:50,640
has always

10
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:52,400
upheld since its establishment.

11
00:01:55,239 --> 00:01:57,280
I will integrate into the team as soon as possible,

12
00:01:57,799 --> 00:01:59,519
to learn and hone

13
00:01:59,519 --> 00:02:00,680
this rigorous work style.

14
00:02:02,079 --> 00:02:03,760
Before coming here, I did some research

15
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:06,159
and learned that our SWAT Detachment's

16
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:08,800
ranking in political work

17
00:02:09,759 --> 00:02:10,479
is less than ideal.

18
00:02:11,479 --> 00:02:12,960
As the new Political Commissar,

19
00:02:13,599 --> 00:02:14,639
I will implement

20
00:02:15,240 --> 00:02:17,159
the Bureau Party Committee's directives,

21
00:02:17,599 --> 00:02:19,159
establish disciplinary red lines,

22
00:02:19,719 --> 00:02:21,120
lead by example,

23
00:02:21,479 --> 00:02:24,759
and integrate political and field work.

24
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:26,240
I have the determination

25
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:27,719
and the confidence

26
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:29,080
that under

27
00:02:29,599 --> 00:02:30,719
the Bureau Party Committee's leadership,

28
00:02:31,599 --> 00:02:32,680
we will build our SWAT Detachment

29
00:02:33,039 --> 00:02:33,759
into a

30
00:02:34,199 --> 00:02:34,800
politically strong,

31
00:02:35,439 --> 00:02:36,080
ideologically strong,

32
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:37,039
organizationally strong,

33
00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:37,719
highly capable,

34
00:02:37,719 --> 00:02:38,479
and strictly disciplined

35
00:02:38,759 --> 00:02:40,560
outstanding citywide SWAT Detachment.

36
00:02:40,639 --> 00:02:41,680
That concludes my speech. Thank you.

37
00:03:00,240 --> 00:03:01,240
What Commissar Tan said

38
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:02,680
was quite sincere.

39
00:03:04,599 --> 00:03:05,800
His points on toughness were spot on.

40
00:03:06,919 --> 00:03:07,560
So I hope

41
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:10,680
under your new commissar's leadership,

42
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:12,719
you will actively support his work.

43
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:15,479
Captain Liao.

44
00:03:16,319 --> 00:03:16,599
Sir!

45
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:18,199
From now on,

46
00:03:19,120 --> 00:03:19,960
whether in life

47
00:03:21,039 --> 00:03:21,879
or at work,

48
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:24,039
I hope you lead the team

49
00:03:24,879 --> 00:03:26,199
to fully cooperate with Commissar Tan.

50
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:27,280
Yes, sir.

51
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:30,000
You see, the SWAT unit

52
00:03:30,479 --> 00:03:31,759
is different from other police branches.

53
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:33,280
They often fall into two extremes.

54
00:03:34,319 --> 00:03:36,120
They don't actually lead investigations,

55
00:03:36,879 --> 00:03:37,280
but

56
00:03:38,159 --> 00:03:39,000
they've all seen life and death.

57
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:41,039
Look at these officers.

58
00:03:41,599 --> 00:03:42,319
They're either very withdrawn

59
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:44,680
or very brash.

60
00:03:45,639 --> 00:03:46,879
So if you stick to

61
00:03:47,120 --> 00:03:48,840
your old methods from the PR Department,

62
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:50,680
they definitely won't work.

63
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:54,400
You really need to think this through.

64
00:03:57,719 --> 00:03:58,560
Do a good job here.

65
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:01,240
I bet

66
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:02,479
he'll open the car door in a minute.

67
00:04:13,599 --> 00:04:13,879
Oh, right.

68
00:04:15,319 --> 00:04:16,319
That little toy of yours

69
00:04:16,959 --> 00:04:17,399
is pretty nice.

70
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:19,079
You can use it

71
00:04:20,199 --> 00:04:20,759
to relieve stress.

72
00:04:28,879 --> 00:04:29,439
Goodbye, Sir.

73
00:04:32,879 --> 00:04:34,800
He sure knows how to kiss up.

74
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:38,079
Well, leaders like that kind of comrade.

75
00:04:38,399 --> 00:04:39,199
What can you do?

76
00:04:41,279 --> 00:04:42,839
It makes my skin crawl.

77
00:04:44,360 --> 00:04:44,959
Just bear with it.

78
00:04:47,519 --> 00:04:48,360
For two years.

79
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:54,800
As for me, with regular training

80
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:56,000
and going on missions,

81
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,439
I spend a lot of time out of the office.

82
00:04:58,079 --> 00:04:58,839
So this room

83
00:04:58,839 --> 00:05:00,040
is basically yours.

84
00:05:04,879 --> 00:05:05,600
The operational work,

85
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:06,800
I'll handle.

86
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:08,680
You handle the rest.

87
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:10,360
All right.

88
00:05:11,199 --> 00:05:11,959
A clear division of labor.

89
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:13,720
As the Political Commissar,

90
00:05:14,079 --> 00:05:15,040
political work

91
00:05:15,199 --> 00:05:16,160
I'll ensure it's done right.

92
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:18,160
As long as it doesn't affect training.

93
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:19,639
Captain Liao,

94
00:05:20,079 --> 00:05:20,759
rest assured.

95
00:05:21,879 --> 00:05:22,639
Strict discipline

96
00:05:23,279 --> 00:05:23,959
and political reliability

97
00:05:24,120 --> 00:05:26,160
are what the SWAT team needs most.

98
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:30,879
We SWAT officers don't chant slogans.

99
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:32,959
We just get things done.

100
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:35,040
We punish mistakes

101
00:05:35,360 --> 00:05:36,480
and reward merits.

102
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:37,319
Understood.

103
00:05:42,519 --> 00:05:43,759
I know you're here to pad your resume.

104
00:05:45,199 --> 00:05:47,439
So I'll cooperate when necessary.

105
00:05:53,160 --> 00:05:55,199
I'll start enforcing discipline tomorrow.

106
00:05:56,360 --> 00:05:57,800
Who's in charge of attendance right now?

107
00:05:58,360 --> 00:05:58,920
Bai Jiani.

108
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:00,439
Just go directly to her.

109
00:06:03,439 --> 00:06:04,360
Also, a reminder,

110
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:06,680
the SWAT team only respects the strong.

111
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:10,120
Respecting the strong is right.

112
00:06:13,319 --> 00:06:14,399
But retaining the strong

113
00:06:15,399 --> 00:06:16,720
is what we leaders must do.

114
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:19,680
I heard

115
00:06:19,959 --> 00:06:22,120
another strong officer was transferred.

116
00:06:22,879 --> 00:06:23,680
Yeah.

117
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:27,839
We urgently must fix the staff turnover.

118
00:06:29,399 --> 00:06:31,160
It was a headache for Commissar Lu,

119
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:36,839
so now we'll leave it to Commissar Tan.

120
00:06:37,560 --> 00:06:39,040
It's no trouble. It's my job.

121
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:40,680
Good.

122
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:08,199
A team always takes after

123
00:07:08,759 --> 00:07:09,759
its leader.

124
00:07:10,439 --> 00:07:12,680
They're all so full of themselves.

125
00:07:13,319 --> 00:07:14,279
They're too hard to manage.

126
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:17,000
Alright.

127
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:17,639
Two years.

128
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:18,839
Just stick it out for two years.

129
00:07:19,839 --> 00:07:20,600
Is that all?

130
00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:22,000
You came to the station just to say this?

131
00:07:23,279 --> 00:07:24,319
There's something else.

132
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:25,879
Shoot.

133
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:27,600
That guy from our SWAT detachment...

134
00:07:28,079 --> 00:07:29,399
that auxiliary cop who came to your unit.

135
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:31,519
Wang Yunsheng.

136
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:32,360
What about him?

137
00:07:32,839 --> 00:07:33,399
How's he doing?

138
00:07:34,879 --> 00:07:35,639
He just got here, you know.

139
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:36,759
What do you expect?

140
00:07:37,480 --> 00:07:38,439
I bet he's not doing great.

141
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:40,639
He doesn't have much experience.

142
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:42,800
Your police station

143
00:07:43,279 --> 00:07:44,279
handles so many trivial matters.

144
00:07:44,839 --> 00:07:46,000
He just transferred over.

145
00:07:47,079 --> 00:07:47,879
It'd be weird if he was doing well.

146
00:07:54,639 --> 00:07:55,000
Of course,

147
00:07:56,319 --> 00:07:57,639
you wanting him

148
00:07:57,639 --> 00:07:58,720
must be for your own reasons.

149
00:08:00,160 --> 00:08:00,759
Get to the point.

150
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:06,439
The SWAT detachment...

151
00:08:07,319 --> 00:08:08,759
this staff turnover issue...

152
00:08:09,319 --> 00:08:09,759
is very serious.

153
00:08:11,199 --> 00:08:13,199
Of course, it's a long-standing issue.

154
00:08:13,759 --> 00:08:15,759
It's not my fault as the new commissar.

155
00:08:17,240 --> 00:08:18,240
But this kid leaving...

156
00:08:19,360 --> 00:08:20,079
the timing...

157
00:08:21,600 --> 00:08:22,319
is a bit coincidental.

158
00:08:22,759 --> 00:08:24,360
Even more coincidental is him coming here.

159
00:08:27,199 --> 00:08:29,519
I'm worried morale will crumble,

160
00:08:29,519 --> 00:08:30,160
making them hard to rally.

161
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:35,159
Do you know Wang Yunsheng?

162
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:37,440
I haven't

163
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:40,200
had a deep talk with him yet.

164
00:08:41,399 --> 00:08:43,399
He requested the transfer here himself.

165
00:08:43,840 --> 00:08:45,080
And he's not young anymore.

166
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:47,120
He still doesn't have a permanent spot.

167
00:08:47,480 --> 00:08:48,480
If he stayed at your unit,

168
00:08:48,480 --> 00:08:50,600
he'd have no chance to become a regular.

169
00:08:51,080 --> 00:08:52,399
The police station is his last hope.

170
00:09:01,519 --> 00:09:02,639
You're afraid

171
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:05,039
others will think we planned this,

172
00:09:06,039 --> 00:09:07,919
intentionally poaching from the SWAT team.

173
00:09:08,559 --> 00:09:08,960
Right?

174
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:12,320
What does it have to do with us?

175
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:16,080
That kid requested to come here himself.

176
00:09:17,080 --> 00:09:18,000
If anyone thinks that way,

177
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:20,120
I'll have to set them straight.

178
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:24,879
Whether Wang Yunsheng leaves or stays

179
00:09:24,879 --> 00:09:26,279
is entirely up to him, right?

180
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:27,200
Yeah.

181
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:28,960
If he wants to leave,

182
00:09:29,559 --> 00:09:30,159
I won't stop him.

183
00:09:35,759 --> 00:09:36,240
Where is he?

184
00:09:37,639 --> 00:09:38,720
I said, where is Wang Yunsheng?

185
00:09:38,799 --> 00:09:39,759
Is he... at the station?

186
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:44,919
He should be back from patrol.

187
00:09:56,399 --> 00:09:56,720
Brother Zhi

188
00:09:58,039 --> 00:09:58,919
Does this count as a merit?

189
00:09:59,200 --> 00:09:59,919
It absolutely counts.

190
00:10:00,279 --> 00:10:00,720
A major one.

191
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:01,960
You saved two lives.

192
00:10:02,039 --> 00:10:03,039
I'll report it to the chief right now.

193
00:10:03,320 --> 00:10:03,840
Alright, you...

194
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:04,639
hurry and wash up.

195
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:05,519
Don't catch a cold.

196
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:16,559
Wang Yunsheng.

197
00:10:16,639 --> 00:10:16,879
Here!

198
00:10:20,080 --> 00:10:20,360
Chief Tan.

199
00:10:22,320 --> 00:10:23,399
I've been transferred to your SWAT team.

200
00:10:25,399 --> 00:10:25,879
As the Political Commissar.

201
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:28,799
Commissar Tan.

202
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:31,639
How did you get covered in mud?

203
00:10:33,039 --> 00:10:34,759
Just now, while patrolling with Zhi,

204
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:36,200
I jumped in the river to save two people.

205
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:38,000
You stepped up and saved lives.

206
00:10:39,159 --> 00:10:40,559
We need to promote this properly.

207
00:10:40,759 --> 00:10:42,200
As an auxiliary police officer,

208
00:10:42,519 --> 00:10:44,639
it's truly commendable that you did this.

209
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:47,039
I heard from Director Ji

210
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:49,799
that they haven't sorted out your dorm yet.

211
00:10:50,919 --> 00:10:51,960
Let's head back to the SWAT detachment.

212
00:10:52,399 --> 00:10:53,360
I'll arrange it for you as the Commissar.

213
00:10:53,559 --> 00:10:53,879
There's no need.

214
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:55,639
I'll just get a room nearby to wash up.

215
00:10:55,639 --> 00:10:57,039
What do you mean get a room?

216
00:10:57,039 --> 00:10:59,120
How much do you even make a month?

217
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:01,200
Don't you want to save up for a family?

218
00:11:01,519 --> 00:11:02,200
Come on, let's go.

219
00:11:02,639 --> 00:11:03,240
I'll arrange it for you.

220
00:11:04,799 --> 00:11:05,200
I'm not going back.

221
00:11:08,080 --> 00:11:09,519
I didn't say I was transferring you back.

222
00:11:09,639 --> 00:11:10,279
Don't overthink it.

223
00:11:12,559 --> 00:11:13,960
There's a free dorm here.

224
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:15,720
Isn't that a good thing?

225
00:11:19,320 --> 00:11:20,080
Do you want to become a regular officer?

226
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:22,480
I've checked with Director Ji

227
00:11:22,799 --> 00:11:23,879
about your situation.

228
00:11:24,039 --> 00:11:24,840
Don't forget what my

229
00:11:24,840 --> 00:11:25,720
previous job was.

230
00:11:26,919 --> 00:11:28,639
We'll talk about making you a regular.

231
00:11:30,519 --> 00:11:32,480
I put that thing in the honors room.

232
00:11:33,080 --> 00:11:34,639
I did it just to piss him off.

233
00:11:35,399 --> 00:11:36,159
Awesome.

234
00:11:37,320 --> 00:11:38,639
Not only did I piss him off,

235
00:11:39,120 --> 00:11:40,159
I even did it right to his face

236
00:11:40,720 --> 00:11:42,159
and called him Commissar Lu.

237
00:11:43,320 --> 00:11:43,879
Xiao.

238
00:11:44,559 --> 00:11:45,799
What was his expression like then?

239
00:11:45,879 --> 00:11:46,960
Yeah, what was his expression?

240
00:11:47,840 --> 00:11:48,360
Lu Xiao.

241
00:11:49,919 --> 00:11:51,600
Stop pulling these

242
00:11:51,639 --> 00:11:52,240
petty tricks in the future.

243
00:11:53,399 --> 00:11:53,799
Yes, sir.

244
00:11:57,759 --> 00:11:59,399
Look who I brought back.

245
00:12:01,519 --> 00:12:01,879
Where is he?

246
00:12:02,919 --> 00:12:03,440
Wang Yunsheng.

247
00:12:03,919 --> 00:12:04,240
Come on.

248
00:12:05,159 --> 00:12:05,960
Wang Yunsheng is back.

249
00:12:09,919 --> 00:12:10,840
Looking so down and out.

250
00:12:12,240 --> 00:12:13,519
What do you mean down and out?

251
00:12:14,840 --> 00:12:16,120
Yunsheng jumped into the river

252
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:17,320
and saved two people.

253
00:12:17,440 --> 00:12:18,360
He risked his life to save others.

254
00:12:18,639 --> 00:12:19,320
Not bad.

255
00:12:19,639 --> 00:12:20,440
You've become a hero.

256
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:22,840
Why isn't the station pampering you?

257
00:12:23,159 --> 00:12:24,000
Why did you come running back here?

258
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:25,799
He was just seconded there.

259
00:12:25,799 --> 00:12:27,360
He's still part of our SWAT detachment.

260
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:28,960
The police station

261
00:12:29,279 --> 00:12:31,759
hasn't sorted out his dorm yet.

262
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:33,840
So I told him to stay here for now.

263
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:35,279
No, I'll just take a shower and leave.

264
00:12:35,519 --> 00:12:36,159
Where are you going?

265
00:12:36,799 --> 00:12:37,639
Since you're back,

266
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:39,279
just stay here.

267
00:12:39,600 --> 00:12:39,919
You see,

268
00:12:40,039 --> 00:12:40,879
Captain Liao has spoken.

269
00:12:41,279 --> 00:12:41,639
Stay here.

270
00:12:42,919 --> 00:12:43,840
Back to your old room.

271
00:12:44,159 --> 00:12:45,279
Our room is full.

272
00:12:46,039 --> 00:12:47,240
Isn't the end room empty?

273
00:12:47,240 --> 00:12:48,000
He can stay there if he wants.

274
00:12:48,960 --> 00:12:50,679
That room is for storage.

275
00:12:53,399 --> 00:12:54,159
He can stay in my room.

276
00:12:55,440 --> 00:12:56,919
Which room did Commissar Lu stay in?

277
00:12:57,240 --> 00:12:57,879
He shared a room with me.

278
00:13:00,080 --> 00:13:00,759
That's not appropriate.

279
00:13:01,279 --> 00:13:02,919
Your schedules are different.

280
00:13:02,919 --> 00:13:04,279
You'd disturb each other's rest.

281
00:13:05,039 --> 00:13:06,080
Just take the room at the end of the hall.

282
00:13:06,519 --> 00:13:07,200
Clean it up,

283
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:08,639
and move in.

284
00:13:09,279 --> 00:13:09,679
No problem.

285
00:13:11,759 --> 00:13:12,679
Go take a shower now, hurry up.

286
00:13:21,919 --> 00:13:22,320
How about it?

287
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:23,399
I got him back, didn't I?

288
00:13:24,600 --> 00:13:26,039
Does just coming back to sleep count?

289
00:13:26,720 --> 00:13:27,840
At least it temporarily solves

290
00:13:27,840 --> 00:13:29,559
the problem of nighttime talent drain.

291
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:31,240
As long as he's physically here,

292
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:32,759
are we afraid his heart won't follow?

293
00:13:56,399 --> 00:13:56,679
Captain Liao.

294
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:01,039
Still doing things the old way.

295
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:15,759
Have a seat.

296
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:16,399
Yes, sir.

297
00:14:23,679 --> 00:14:25,320
The local station is busier, right?

298
00:14:26,519 --> 00:14:27,200
There's quite a lot to do.

299
00:14:27,919 --> 00:14:28,519
Definitely.

300
00:14:29,399 --> 00:14:31,399
Even though it's mostly trivial stuff,

301
00:14:32,559 --> 00:14:33,840
handling it can still be quite

302
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:35,159
draining.

303
00:14:39,159 --> 00:14:40,639
Born in the Year of the Horse, right?

304
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:42,240
You're 29 this year.

305
00:14:45,279 --> 00:14:45,840
Twenty-nine.

306
00:14:48,679 --> 00:14:50,120
In one year, you'll be over the age limit.

307
00:14:57,159 --> 00:14:58,240
You need to work hard,

308
00:14:59,679 --> 00:15:02,200
try to get commended soon,

309
00:15:02,639 --> 00:15:03,639
pass the exam,

310
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:04,759
and become official.

311
00:15:10,240 --> 00:15:11,600
Now that you've moved back in,

312
00:15:12,799 --> 00:15:13,440
as for your training,

313
00:15:14,639 --> 00:15:15,360
don't let it slide.

314
00:15:16,399 --> 00:15:18,080
Your skills belong to you.

315
00:15:19,039 --> 00:15:20,200
If you need anything, just let me know.

316
00:15:21,399 --> 00:15:21,759
Yes, sir.

317
00:15:26,399 --> 00:15:26,840
This place...

318
00:15:30,519 --> 00:15:31,720
tidy it up a bit later.

319
00:15:32,799 --> 00:15:34,000
It'll be more comfortable to live in.

320
00:15:49,879 --> 00:15:50,600
Go to bed early.

321
00:15:51,960 --> 00:15:53,039
Breakfast is at the usual time.

322
00:15:53,440 --> 00:15:53,759
Yes.

323
00:16:38,679 --> 00:16:39,240
Boss.

324
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:43,399
Your shop keeps opening and closing.

325
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:45,159
Boss.

326
00:16:45,960 --> 00:16:46,799
A pack of gum, please.

327
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:48,120
Sorry about that.

328
00:16:48,120 --> 00:16:49,440
We're not officially open yet.

329
00:16:52,440 --> 00:16:53,159
Captain Liao.

330
00:16:53,960 --> 00:16:54,919
What are you doing here?

331
00:16:55,759 --> 00:16:57,120
During our chat last time,

332
00:16:57,399 --> 00:16:58,080
you said

333
00:16:58,559 --> 00:16:59,559
if I felt unsafe,

334
00:16:59,679 --> 00:17:01,200
I should find a place that feels safe.

335
00:17:01,840 --> 00:17:02,759
I went back and thought about it.

336
00:17:02,840 --> 00:17:04,480
There's truly nowhere

337
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:05,400
safer than right outside your gates.

338
00:17:05,880 --> 00:17:07,279
This shop happened to be for sublease,

339
00:17:07,279 --> 00:17:08,079
so I took it over.

340
00:17:10,279 --> 00:17:11,559
Lu Xiao was just saying that offhand.

341
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:12,799
Under normal circumstances,

342
00:17:12,799 --> 00:17:14,000
you just need some time to process it.

343
00:17:14,319 --> 00:17:15,559
I've already signed the lease.

344
00:17:16,759 --> 00:17:18,319
Besides, opening a shop here

345
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:19,039
makes it convenient for you guys too.

346
00:17:19,920 --> 00:17:20,359
That's true.

347
00:17:21,640 --> 00:17:21,920
Yeah.

348
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:23,440
I haven't stocked the gum yet.

349
00:17:23,839 --> 00:17:24,960
But I think I have a pack here.

350
00:17:25,039 --> 00:17:25,440
No, no, it's fine.

351
00:17:25,440 --> 00:17:26,400
It's opened but untouched.

352
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:27,200
No need, thanks. Thank you.

353
00:17:27,839 --> 00:17:29,680
I just saw the lights were on,

354
00:17:29,680 --> 00:17:30,480
so I came over to take a look.

355
00:17:31,519 --> 00:17:32,559
We're neighbors now.

356
00:17:33,079 --> 00:17:34,240
Just let me know if you need anything.

357
00:17:35,400 --> 00:17:36,440
It really is safe here.

358
00:17:37,559 --> 00:17:39,039
The cameras at our gate catch everything.

359
00:17:40,279 --> 00:17:41,079
Mom.

360
00:17:42,160 --> 00:17:42,519
Naonao.

361
00:17:43,599 --> 00:17:43,880
Come here.

362
00:17:45,079 --> 00:17:45,960
You just woke up.

363
00:17:47,079 --> 00:17:48,400
Say hi to Uncle Liao.

364
00:17:49,279 --> 00:17:50,000
Do you still remember me?

365
00:18:03,720 --> 00:18:04,400
For me?

366
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:08,440
Thanks.

367
00:18:44,960 --> 00:18:45,480
Morning, Commissar Tan.

368
00:18:45,960 --> 00:18:46,240
Morning.

369
00:18:58,640 --> 00:18:59,000
Seven o'clock sharp.

370
00:19:01,240 --> 00:19:02,480
So you're the only one on time.

371
00:19:05,880 --> 00:19:08,039
Mark everyone else as absent.

372
00:19:08,519 --> 00:19:09,119
Including Captain Liao.

373
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:10,960
Reporting, Commissar.

374
00:19:11,599 --> 00:19:13,119
Today's morning drill was at 6:30.

375
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:15,920
Who changed it?

376
00:19:16,680 --> 00:19:17,119
Captain Liao.

377
00:19:18,519 --> 00:19:19,680
Train your body,

378
00:19:19,839 --> 00:19:21,160
Train your body,

379
00:19:21,319 --> 00:19:22,519
Stay sharp and ready!

380
00:19:22,680 --> 00:19:23,880
Build your muscles,

381
00:19:24,039 --> 00:19:25,359
Ready to take a beating!

382
00:19:25,480 --> 00:19:26,519
One, two, one.

383
00:19:26,839 --> 00:19:27,440
Halt!

384
00:19:28,039 --> 00:19:28,440
Dismissed!

385
00:19:34,519 --> 00:19:34,839
Morning.

386
00:19:35,400 --> 00:19:35,720
Captain Liao.

387
00:19:36,319 --> 00:19:36,519
Morning.

388
00:19:39,200 --> 00:19:39,960
Morning, Commissar.

389
00:19:40,799 --> 00:19:41,000
Morning.

390
00:19:44,839 --> 00:19:46,240
I thought morning drill was at seven.

391
00:19:46,880 --> 00:19:47,839
Flexible morning drill.

392
00:19:52,359 --> 00:19:53,480
Next time you change the schedule,

393
00:19:53,480 --> 00:19:54,759
could you let me know in advance?

394
00:19:56,480 --> 00:19:58,000
The SWAT team follows the whistle.

395
00:19:59,519 --> 00:19:59,960
Bai Jiani!

396
00:19:59,960 --> 00:20:00,200
Here!

397
00:20:00,680 --> 00:20:02,319
Commissar Tan follows the 8 AM schedule.

398
00:20:02,599 --> 00:20:03,720
No, seven is fine.

399
00:20:04,119 --> 00:20:04,759
It's no problem.

400
00:20:05,960 --> 00:20:06,839
Absent, Tan Yan.

401
00:20:06,960 --> 00:20:07,160
Mark it down.

402
00:20:07,960 --> 00:20:08,200
Yes, sir.

403
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:22,160
I'm taking the assault team this morning

404
00:20:22,160 --> 00:20:23,599
to the beach for a physical assessment.

405
00:20:23,880 --> 00:20:25,240
I'll leave the patrol duties to you.

406
00:20:25,240 --> 00:20:26,880
You assign the patrols for all four zones.

407
00:20:27,599 --> 00:20:28,839
Follow Level 3 security protocols.

408
00:20:29,119 --> 00:20:29,480
Got it.

409
00:20:29,759 --> 00:20:31,440
No need to go this afternoon. I've got it.

410
00:20:42,279 --> 00:20:42,759
Commissar.

411
00:20:43,880 --> 00:20:46,200
You used to work at the agency,

412
00:20:46,200 --> 00:20:47,119
so you must have been very busy.

413
00:20:47,559 --> 00:20:49,240
Now that you suddenly have free time,

414
00:20:49,640 --> 00:20:50,680
will you find it hard to adjust?

415
00:20:59,200 --> 00:21:01,400
Actually, you won't be idle here either.

416
00:21:02,519 --> 00:21:04,599
You're in charge of their daily lives.

417
00:21:05,880 --> 00:21:06,680
I'll get back to work.

418
00:21:08,440 --> 00:21:08,960
Go ahead.

419
00:21:12,240 --> 00:21:13,400
Am I really that idle?

420
00:21:23,319 --> 00:21:25,480
What are you guys up to?

421
00:21:26,160 --> 00:21:27,079
Do you have any cases

422
00:21:27,079 --> 00:21:29,240
that need the SWAT team's support?

423
00:21:30,200 --> 00:21:31,359
These kids in the SWAT team

424
00:21:31,640 --> 00:21:33,799
all think I'm a slacker.

425
00:21:34,519 --> 00:21:35,759
I'm pretty frustrated about it.

426
00:21:36,519 --> 00:21:38,960
Today isn't just a fitness test,

427
00:21:39,440 --> 00:21:41,279
it's about pushing past your limits!

428
00:21:41,640 --> 00:21:43,640
Spicy girls, spicy! Spicy girls, spicy!

429
00:21:43,799 --> 00:21:46,200
Spicy girls, spicy, spicy, spicy, spicy!

430
00:21:48,559 --> 00:21:49,039
Eight Meals.

431
00:21:50,160 --> 00:21:51,359
Eating eight meals a day.

432
00:21:54,240 --> 00:21:54,799
Pudding.

433
00:21:58,559 --> 00:21:59,880
You must be Pudding.

434
00:22:01,240 --> 00:22:02,960
I'm Tan Yan, the new Commissar.

435
00:22:09,720 --> 00:22:10,519
Director Yu.

436
00:22:18,039 --> 00:22:18,480
Director Yu.

437
00:22:19,079 --> 00:22:20,759
I'm busy right now. Yes, yes, yes.

438
00:22:21,640 --> 00:22:22,920
The SWAT team is so busy.

439
00:22:23,279 --> 00:22:23,839
I didn't hear you.

440
00:22:24,200 --> 00:22:24,920
Go ahead, speak.

441
00:22:26,920 --> 00:22:28,000
If it weren't for Captain Liao

442
00:22:28,440 --> 00:22:29,319
firing decisively,

443
00:22:29,880 --> 00:22:31,160
the consequences would've been disastrous.

444
00:22:32,240 --> 00:22:33,920
I was at the scene.

445
00:22:34,920 --> 00:22:35,839
Objectively speaking,

446
00:22:36,920 --> 00:22:39,039
the success of that hostage rescue

447
00:22:39,559 --> 00:22:42,240
relied on the teamwork of the SWAT members.

448
00:22:42,319 --> 00:22:42,640
That's true.

449
00:22:45,480 --> 00:22:47,839
I feel like a collective third-class merit

450
00:22:48,359 --> 00:22:49,079
might be more appropriate.

451
00:22:51,519 --> 00:22:52,000
Commissar Tan,

452
00:22:53,480 --> 00:22:54,640
the Bureau Party Committee decided this

453
00:22:54,880 --> 00:22:57,319
decided after careful discussion.

454
00:22:59,759 --> 00:23:00,680
Personally, I believe that

455
00:23:00,680 --> 00:23:02,359
whether it's collective or individual,

456
00:23:03,359 --> 00:23:06,119
it's an acknowledgment of your SWAT team.

457
00:23:11,440 --> 00:23:13,079
There is still some difference.

458
00:23:14,240 --> 00:23:15,559
Collective honor

459
00:23:16,039 --> 00:23:17,160
for the SWAT team,

460
00:23:17,559 --> 00:23:18,960
in my opinion, is more important.

461
00:23:21,400 --> 00:23:21,880
How about this?

462
00:23:23,680 --> 00:23:25,640
Go talk to the bureau leaders again.

463
00:23:26,599 --> 00:23:27,240
This thing

464
00:23:28,359 --> 00:23:29,119
can stay with me for now.

465
00:23:29,720 --> 00:23:30,519
I'll hold onto it for you.

466
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:34,519
No, Director Yu,

467
00:23:35,599 --> 00:23:36,519
you misunderstood me.

468
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:37,720
You're right.

469
00:23:38,640 --> 00:23:40,519
Whether it's individual or collective,

470
00:23:41,240 --> 00:23:42,839
it's an acknowledgment of us.

471
00:23:44,759 --> 00:23:45,200
Alright then.

472
00:23:45,880 --> 00:23:46,920
Then I can only

473
00:23:47,160 --> 00:23:47,720
leave this to you.

474
00:23:49,000 --> 00:23:50,119
Rest assured, Director Yu.

475
00:23:50,799 --> 00:23:52,599
I also have a background in political work.

476
00:23:52,599 --> 00:23:55,160
I'll make sure it's handled beautifully.

477
00:23:57,640 --> 00:23:57,960
Okay.

478
00:24:04,319 --> 00:24:04,640
Commissar Tan.

479
00:24:07,359 --> 00:24:08,240
Everyone's busy.

480
00:24:08,240 --> 00:24:08,920
Commissar Tan.

481
00:24:10,359 --> 00:24:11,319
Is Chief Zhao busy?

482
00:24:11,599 --> 00:24:12,319
He's inside.

483
00:24:12,599 --> 00:24:13,720
Okay, I know. Have a seat.

484
00:24:14,680 --> 00:24:15,519
No, no, no, that's fine.

485
00:24:20,839 --> 00:24:21,680
I'll keep that in mind.

486
00:24:22,720 --> 00:24:23,079
Don't worry.

487
00:24:24,400 --> 00:24:25,119
Okay, sounds good.

488
00:24:27,440 --> 00:24:28,400
What brings you here?

489
00:24:29,119 --> 00:24:29,640
Commissar Tan.

490
00:24:29,720 --> 00:24:30,559
I'm here on some business.

491
00:24:30,559 --> 00:24:31,160
And to visit you.

492
00:24:32,599 --> 00:24:33,680
Come, come in. Quick.

493
00:24:33,759 --> 00:24:34,039
Come.

494
00:24:35,839 --> 00:24:36,559
Busy, huh?

495
00:24:37,519 --> 00:24:38,519
Tell me about it.

496
00:24:39,079 --> 00:24:40,240
When you were here,

497
00:24:40,240 --> 00:24:42,599
I never felt the PR Department was busy.

498
00:24:43,079 --> 00:24:44,039
Now that you've transferred,

499
00:24:44,319 --> 00:24:45,680
even if you split me in half right now,

500
00:24:45,680 --> 00:24:46,720
it still wouldn't be enough.

501
00:24:50,319 --> 00:24:50,920
Director Zhao,

502
00:24:51,240 --> 00:24:52,799
if you ever need my help,

503
00:24:52,799 --> 00:24:53,640
just let me know.

504
00:24:53,880 --> 00:24:55,680
A call or WeChat works.

505
00:24:56,039 --> 00:24:56,400
Right.

506
00:24:57,480 --> 00:24:58,440
Like I said before,

507
00:24:58,839 --> 00:25:00,680
if you need anything at the SWAT team,

508
00:25:00,960 --> 00:25:01,640
just say the word.

509
00:25:03,759 --> 00:25:05,680
I came to see you because I need a favor.

510
00:25:06,240 --> 00:25:06,920
What is it? Just say it.

511
00:25:08,119 --> 00:25:10,240
Because of that hostage case,

512
00:25:10,400 --> 00:25:12,839
the Party Committee decided to award Liao

513
00:25:13,400 --> 00:25:14,559
a Personal Third-Class Merit.

514
00:25:15,640 --> 00:25:17,880
I was wondering if the police magazine

515
00:25:18,559 --> 00:25:19,319
could...

516
00:25:19,559 --> 00:25:20,759
No problem. This is a good thing.

517
00:25:21,319 --> 00:25:22,359
I'll reserve the space for you.

518
00:25:24,279 --> 00:25:24,640
How's that?

519
00:25:25,079 --> 00:25:25,920
Thank you, Director Zhao.

520
00:25:29,880 --> 00:25:30,680
The thing is,

521
00:25:33,480 --> 00:25:36,559
due to Comrade Lu Zhong's sacrifice,

522
00:25:37,200 --> 00:25:39,680
the SWAT detachment's morale has been low.

523
00:25:40,559 --> 00:25:42,400
I want to use this Third-Class Merit

524
00:25:43,000 --> 00:25:45,359
to boost their morale.

525
00:25:46,759 --> 00:25:48,839
Just space isn't enough.

526
00:25:50,519 --> 00:25:51,480
I get it.

527
00:25:52,680 --> 00:25:54,039
This doesn't just need ordinary publicity.

528
00:25:54,519 --> 00:25:56,200
It needs to be heavily promoted.

529
00:25:57,480 --> 00:25:59,200
I'll give this issue's cover to the SWAT.

530
00:26:00,279 --> 00:26:00,680
How does that sound?

531
00:26:01,640 --> 00:26:02,319
Director Zhao.

532
00:26:02,680 --> 00:26:04,880
On behalf of the SWAT team, thank you.

533
00:26:05,480 --> 00:26:06,880
Don't mention it. It's my job.

534
00:26:30,200 --> 00:26:31,519
275

535
00:26:32,279 --> 00:26:33,400
275

536
00:26:37,119 --> 00:26:37,839
Sir.

537
00:26:39,240 --> 00:26:40,359
So it's you.

538
00:26:41,359 --> 00:26:42,720
You work at the SWAT base too?

539
00:26:43,559 --> 00:26:44,319
I remember you.

540
00:26:44,799 --> 00:26:45,119
Aren't you...

541
00:26:45,119 --> 00:26:46,599
Are you working here, or...

542
00:26:46,680 --> 00:26:48,680
We just took over this shop.

543
00:26:50,759 --> 00:26:52,000
You're the boss now. What's your name?

544
00:26:52,160 --> 00:26:53,119
Just call me Xiao Yuan.

545
00:26:53,319 --> 00:26:53,920
Xiao Yuan.

546
00:26:54,160 --> 00:26:54,880
My last name is Tan.

547
00:26:56,480 --> 00:26:57,279
I was just transferred here

548
00:26:57,279 --> 00:26:59,200
as the SWAT team's Political Commissar.

549
00:27:00,119 --> 00:27:01,799
Why did you open a shop here?

550
00:27:03,680 --> 00:27:05,240
Well, after that incident...

551
00:27:05,920 --> 00:27:07,400
I've been feeling uneasy.

552
00:27:07,759 --> 00:27:09,359
It's just me and my son, so we figured

553
00:27:09,559 --> 00:27:11,480
it's safest right by the SWAT base.

554
00:27:12,440 --> 00:27:13,359
Thank you, sir,

555
00:27:13,720 --> 00:27:14,880
for standing up for us.

556
00:27:15,240 --> 00:27:16,319
No need to thank me.

557
00:27:16,319 --> 00:27:17,279
We're police officers.

558
00:27:17,400 --> 00:27:19,559
The safety of people's lives and property

559
00:27:19,680 --> 00:27:20,480
comes above all else.

560
00:27:21,039 --> 00:27:21,519
How much is it?

561
00:27:21,920 --> 00:27:23,160
Really, I can't take your money.

562
00:27:23,160 --> 00:27:24,200
I've been looking for an opportunity

563
00:27:24,200 --> 00:27:24,960
to thank you all.

564
00:27:24,960 --> 00:27:25,599
That won't do.

565
00:27:25,599 --> 00:27:26,839
I really can't take your money.

566
00:27:27,000 --> 00:27:27,759
Commissar Tan, really.

567
00:27:27,759 --> 00:27:28,960
Don't be so polite.

568
00:27:29,160 --> 00:27:29,960
This little bit of stuff

569
00:27:30,079 --> 00:27:30,759
is nothing.

570
00:27:31,240 --> 00:27:32,440
We're neighbors now.

571
00:27:32,440 --> 00:27:33,319
We have plenty of time ahead.

572
00:27:33,440 --> 00:27:34,039
Plenty of time ahead.

573
00:27:35,519 --> 00:27:36,720
Is this your son?

574
00:27:36,839 --> 00:27:37,359
What's his name?

575
00:27:38,880 --> 00:27:39,440
Naonao.

576
00:27:40,319 --> 00:27:41,119
Look who it is.

577
00:27:41,599 --> 00:27:42,559
Say hi to Uncle Tan.

